Package: oneplus-erhai-pen
Version: 0.5
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: TheMojoMan <themojoman@gmx.net>
Depends: bluez, python3-gi
Description: OnePlus pen (stylus) support for the OnePlus Pad 3 (erhai)
 Linux/BlueZ port of the stock OxygenOS "OplusPen" service
 (org.lineageos.pen in the LineageOS erhai open-source tree).  Auto-pairs,
 trusts and connects the OnePlus pen over Bluetooth (BLE HID, Goodix OUI
 F8:6F:DE / Maxeye OUI C0:87:06, HID vendor 22D9/330A) and keeps
 /run/erhai-pen/{state,addr,soc} current.  Since 0.2 it toasts the pen's
 state of charge for 5 s when the pen is attached to / detached from the
 tablet's charging coil (kernel +b10, oplus_cps8601 debugfs).  Since 0.3 the
 percentage itself is read from the pen over Bluetooth (GATT Battery Service
 0x180F / Battery Level 0x2A19, published as /run/erhai-pen/soc) -- the same
 source stock Android's charger HAL feeds the driver as the writable rx_soc
 attribute -- so the toast shows the real value instead of the coil's 0.
 Since 0.4 the monitor watches the CPS8601 charger for the pen's ATTACH edge
 and starts a BLE scan + reconnect the moment the pen is placed on the coil
 (the coil is what wakes the pen's radio), learning the pen's BLE MAC from the
 coil for instant reconnects; new `erhai-pen charger` CLI.  Since 0.5 the
 monitor also feeds the pen's BLE SoC into the coil driver's writable rx_soc
 knob, so the driver stops charging the pen at 100% and re-arms charging once
 the pen has drained below the threshold (kernel +b17).  The pen
 tip/position/pressure path stays in the NT36536 in-cell digitizer (touch
 driver), as on stock.  Package README:
 /usr/share/oneplus-erhai-pen/README.md
